Method Endpoint Description <code>GET</code> <code>/api/lists/{name}</code> Get the content of a list, where {name} is the name of the list to get. <p>Example request:</p> <pre><code>curl -k -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;" https://localhost:8080/api/lists/my-list
</code></pre> <p>Example response:</p> <pre><code>{
  "items": [
    "item1",
    "item2"
  ],
  "description": "My description"
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>items</code> - The list's items.</li> <li><code>description</code> - The list's description, or an empty string if it has none.</li> </ul>

Method Endpoint Description <code>GET</code> <code>/api/models</code> List the local models. <p>Example request:</p> <pre><code>curl -k -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;" https://localhost:8080/api/models
</code></pre> <p>Example response:</p> <pre><code>{
  "models": [
    {
      "encoder": "microsoft/deberta-v3-xsmall",
      "maxLength": 512,
      "maxWidth": 12,
      "name": "pii-en-xsmall",
      "sizeBytes": 98724945
    }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>name</code> - The name a policy gives as <code>modelPath</code>.</li> <li><code>encoder</code> - The encoder the model was trained from, from its <code>gliner_config.json</code>. Absent when the configuration does not say.</li> <li><code>maxLength</code> - The most words of a text the model reads; later words are not examined. Absent when the configuration does not say.</li> <li><code>maxWidth</code> - The most words one detected entity can span. Absent when the configuration does not say.</li> <li><code>sizeBytes</code> - The combined size of its <code>gliner_config.json</code>, <code>tokenizer.json</code>, and <code>model.onnx</code>.</li> </ul> <p>Models are ordered by name. A subdirectory missing one of the files, or whose <code>gliner_config.json</code> cannot be read, is not listed.</p> <ul> <li><code>200 OK</code> - Every model, which may be none.</li> </ul>

Method Endpoint Description <code>GET</code> <code>/api/policies/{policyName}</code> Get the content of a policy, where {policyName} is the name of the policy to get. <p>A name beginning with <code>managed_</code> returns that managed policy. The response is the policy itself; its description and notes are returned by Get a Policy's Details.</p> <p>The <code>ETag</code> response header identifies the policy as read, together with its description and notes, such as <code>"7-0123456789abcdef"</code>. Send it back in <code>If-Match</code> when you change the policy; see Preventing lost updates. A read that sends it in <code>If-None-Match</code> gets <code>304 Not Modified</code>, with no body, while the policy and its details are unchanged.</p> <p>Example request:</p> <pre><code>curl -k -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;" https://localhost:8080/api/policies/my-policy
</code></pre> <p>Example response:</p> <pre><code>{
  "name": "just-phone-numbers",
  "ignored": [
  ],
  "identifiers": {
    "dictionaries": [
    ],
    "phoneNumber": {
      "phoneNumberFilterStrategies": [
        {
          "strategy": "REDACT",
          "redactionFormat": "{{{REDACTED-%t}}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

Method Endpoint Description <code>GET</code> <code>/api/policies/templates/{templateName}</code> Get a starting point for a new policy. <p>Returns a template: native policy JSON that Philter accepts for its running policy schema version, to edit and then save with Save a Policy. Use it instead of keeping your own starting policy, which can fall behind the schema as filters are added. Requires <code>policies:read</code>.</p> <p>The template named <code>default</code> is the one every new user's <code>default</code> policy is created from: it is configured to redact person names, Social Security numbers, and email addresses. Names are detected in-process by <code>ph-eye-pii-en-small</code>, the PhEye model the Philter Docker image includes in <code>PHEYE_MODELS_DIRECTORY</code>, at the model's recommended threshold of 0.9; no PhEye service is needed. Outside the image, the policy needs a model by that name in <code>PHEYE_MODELS_DIRECTORY</code> (see the Models API). A template is not a policy, and cannot be used to redact until it is saved as one.</p> <p>Example request:</p> <pre><code>curl -k -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;" https://localhost:8080/api/policies/templates/default
</code></pre> <p>Example response:</p> <pre><code>{
  "identifiers": {
    "person": {
      "phEyeConfiguration": {
        "modelPath": "ph-eye-pii-en-small",
        "labels": ["name"],
        "threshold": 0.9
      },
      "phEyeFilterStrategies": [
        { "strategy": "REDACT" }
      ]
    },
    "ssn": {
      "ssnFilterStrategies": [
        { "strategy": "REDACT" }
      ]
    },
    "emailAddress": {
      "emailAddressFilterStrategies": [
        { "strategy": "REDACT" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li><code>200 OK</code> - The template's policy JSON.</li> <li><code>404 Not Found</code> - There is no template with that name. The message lists the templates there are.</li> </ul>

Method Endpoint Description <code>PUT</code> <code>/api/policies/{policyName}/details</code> Set a policy's description and notes. <p>Requires <code>policies:write</code>. Returns the policy's details.</p> <pre><code>{
  "description": "Federal court filings",
  "notes": ""
}
</code></pre> <p>A field left out is left as it is, and an empty value clears it. The description may be up to 200 characters and the notes up to 1000, in any language. Description and notes are not part of the policy, so changing them does not create a new version, but it does change the policy's <code>etag</code>.</p> <p>Send the <code>ETag</code> from your read in <code>If-Match</code> to make the change conditional; see Preventing lost updates. The response's <code>ETag</code> header identifies the details as written.</p> <ul> <li><code>400 Bad Request</code> - The description or notes are too long, or <code>If-Match</code> is not an entity tag this API returned.</li> <li><code>404 Not Found</code> - There is no such policy.</li> <li><code>409 Conflict</code> - Nothing was changed. The body carries a <code>message</code> and a <code>reason</code>:<ul> <li><code>policy_managed</code> - The policy is a managed policy, which cannot be changed.</li> <li><code>policy_changed</code> - The policy, its description, or its notes changed since the read named in <code>If-Match</code>, or while this request was writing. Read it again and retry.</li> </ul> </li> </ul>

Method Endpoint Description <code>GET</code> <code>/api/redact-lists</code> Get the account's always-redact and never-redact lists. <p>Both lists are always present in the response; an account with no saved terms returns empty arrays. Each list's revision is returned too, for replacing one list.</p> <p>Example request:</p> <pre><code>curl -k -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;" https://localhost:8080/api/redact-lists
</code></pre> <p>Example response:</p> <pre><code>{
  "alwaysRedact": [
    "Project Cardinal",
    "ACME-1234"
  ],
  "neverRedact": [
    "Philterd"
  ],
  "alwaysRedactRevision": 4,
  "neverRedactRevision": 1
}
</code></pre>

Method Endpoint Description <code>GET</code> <code>/api/redact-lists/{list}</code> Get one list and its revision. <p><code>{list}</code> is <code>always</code> or <code>never</code>. Any other value returns <code>404 Not Found</code>. Requires the <code>lists:read</code> scope.</p> <p>The response's <code>ETag</code> header carries the revision, quoted, such as <code>"4"</code>. Send it back as <code>If-Match</code> when replacing the list.</p> <p>Example request:</p> <pre><code>curl -k -i -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;" https://localhost:8080/api/redact-lists/always
</code></pre> <p>Example response:</p> <pre><code>ETag: "4"
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "terms": [
    "Project Cardinal",
    "ACME-1234"
  ],
  "revision": 4
}
</code></pre>
